  project:'About Barik', doc_project:c=>'<h1 class="pg">About Barik</h1><p>Barik (Բառիկ, “little word”) is a website for people learning Eastern Armenian, the language spoken in Armenia. It is an independent project from Yerevan.</p><h2>What is inside</h2><p>20,121 words in 485 topics, translated into English, Russian, French, Spanish, German and Portuguese. An alphabet of 39 letters with handwriting: a pen shows how each letter is written, and you can trace it with your finger. The Pomegranate path has six stages, from the first letters to reading Tumanyan and Teryan in the original: formulas instead of rules, scenes from life in Armenia, and practice built from the dictionary.</p><h2>What it costs</h2><p>Free: the alphabet and handwriting, level A1, the first stages of the path, search across the whole dictionary and the pronunciation of any word. Barik Premium opens living Eastern Armenian of modern Yerevan (levels A2–C2, dialogues, reading Tumanyan with voices Anahit & Hayk): Pro Monthly ($12/mo), Pro Annual ($59/yr — $4.92/mo, save 59%), or Heritage Lifetime ($129 one-time). Payments are handled by Dodo Payments; subscriptions can be cancelled any time in your account.</p><h2>What you will not find</h2><p>Ads, third-party trackers or newsletters. Your progress stays on your device, and an account needs only an email and a nickname.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions, mistakes in words, suggestions: '+c+'.</p>',
  credits:'Sources and licences', doc_credits:c=>'<h1 class="pg">Sources and licences</h1><p>Everything in Barik is our own work except what is listed below. Third-party material is used under its licence, with credit to its authors.</p><h2>Ours</h2><p>The Pomegranate method, formulas and explanations, scenes and dialogues, exercises, translations of words and texts into Russian, English, French, Spanish, German and Portuguese, transcription, word pictures, letter handwriting (lines drawn anew), design and software — © Barik.</p><h2>Dictionary: Armenian words, forms, word families</h2><p>Part of the Armenian words, the declension and conjugation tables (the reference for forms) and the etymology data come from <a href="https://en.wiktionary.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wiktionary</a> (extraction by <a href="https://kaikki.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kaikki.org</a>) under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Changes: selection and checking of words, reformed spelling, our own translations; forms are generated by our software. This dictionary data, with our changes, is shared under the same <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> licence.</p><h2>Reading texts</h2><p>Poems and tales by Hovhannes Tumanyan (1869–1923), Vahan Teryan (1885–1920) and Yeghishe Charents (1897–1937) are in the public domain: the term of protection (70 years after the author’s death) has expired. The Armenian text follows <a href="https://hy.wikisource.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikisource</a>; each lesson links to its source. Translations, notes and exercises are ours.</p><h2>Pictures</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fluentui-emoji" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft Fluent Emoji</a> (3D) — MIT licence, © Microsoft Corporation; licence text: <a href="pics/LICENSE-FluentEmoji.txt" target="_blank">pics/LICENSE-FluentEmoji.txt</a>.</p><h2>Fonts</h2><p>Noto Serif Armenian (© 2022 The Noto Project Authors), Golos Text (© 2019 The Golos Text Project Authors), Manrope (© 2019 The Manrope Project Authors) — SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts: <a href="fonts/OFL-NotoSerifArmenian.txt" target="_blank">OFL-NotoSerifArmenian.txt</a>, <a href="fonts/OFL-GolosText.txt" target="_blank">OFL-GolosText.txt</a>, <a href="fonts/OFL-Manrope.txt" target="_blank">OFL-Manrope.txt</a>.</p><h2>Audio</h2><p>Synthetic voices by Microsoft Azure AI Speech (Armenian hy-AM-AnahitNeural and hy-AM-HaykNeural; translations — ru-RU-SvetlanaNeural, en-US-JennyNeural, fr-FR-DeniseNeural, es-AR-ElenaNeural, de-DE-KatjaNeural, pt-BR-FranciscaNeural), on a paid tier that grants the right to use the recordings commercially. It is not the voice of a real person.</p><h2>If you are a rights holder</h2><p>If you believe material on this site infringes your rights, write to <a href="mailto:'+c+'">'+c+'</a> saying what and where. We will reply and, if the infringement is confirmed, remove the material.</p>',
