  doc_privacy_web:'<h1 class="pg">Privacy policy</h1><p>Barik collects as little as possible about you — only what the account cannot work without.</p><h2>Your account</h2><p>If you create an account, we store your email address, nickname, sign-up and last sign-in dates and, if you subscribe, the subscription status, term and your customer and subscription IDs at Dodo Payments. Before payment we ask for and store your first and last name, date of birth, gender and country: the name and country are passed to Dodo Payments for the receipt and tax, the date of birth confirms your age (subscriptions from 14), gender and country help us understand who learns Armenian. We share them with no one except Dodo Payments. There is no password: a one-time code is sent to your email and only its hash is kept. Your email is used for sign-in codes and — only if you turn them on — for review reminders (unsubscribe with the link in the email); never for newsletters. You can delete the account with all of this data using the "Delete account" button.</p><h2>Learning progress</h2><p>If you are not signed in, your progress is stored only in the browser on your device. If you sign in, your progress (which words and lessons you have done, and when) is also saved on our server, so that it is not lost and is available on your other devices; it is deleted together with the account. Settings and flagged words stay on the device. Signing in sets one technical cookie — no advertising, no tracking.</p><h2>Payments</h2><p>The subscription is sold and payments are processed by Dodo Payments (dodopayments.com), our merchant of record. Payment details are entered on the Dodo Payments checkout page and are never available to us; how Dodo Payments handles them is described in its privacy policy at dodopayments.com.</p><h2>Advertising and analytics</h2><p>No advertising and no third-party counters. The site counts visits itself and only as daily totals: how many people opened it, in which language, from which country (by the device’s time zone), where they came from and which sections they used. No cookies, no stored IP addresses and no link to your account. Checkout takes place on the Dodo Payments page.</p><h2>Mistake reports and Telegram</h2><p>A "Mistake in this word?" report reaches us as the word, the site language, what is wrong and your comment (if you wrote one), plus your account number if you are signed in; it is used only to fix the dictionary. If you subscribe to the "word of the day" Telegram bot, we store the chat ID and the language you chose; the /stop command unsubscribes you.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about your data — to the address listed on barik.am.</p>',
  doc_terms_web:'<h1 class="pg">Terms of use</h1><p>Free: the alphabet, level A1 words, the first two stages of the Pomegranate path, search across the whole dictionary and pronunciation. The Barik Premium subscription unlocks the words of levels A2–C2 and the remaining stages of the path. During the launch period paid material may be temporarily open to everyone.</p><h2>Subscription</h2><p>You can choose Pro Monthly ($12/month), Pro Annual ($59/year — $4.92/month), or a one-time Heritage Lifetime purchase ($129, no renewal) in your account. Payments are handled by Dodo Payments, the merchant of record: it issues the receipt and handles taxes. The subscription renews automatically until you cancel it: "Account" → "Manage subscription"; access remains until the end of the paid period. Refunds are available within 14 days of a charge; see “Refunds and cancellation”. Payment questions: hello@barik.am.</p><h2>Account</h2><p>One account per person. A nickname must not be offensive or impersonate someone else — we may change such a nickname.</p><h2>Content</h2><p>The dictionary is made for learning Eastern Armenian in reformed spelling. We try to avoid mistakes; if you find one, flag the word with the "Mistake in this word?" button. The audio is a synthetic voice by Microsoft Azure.</p><h2>Rights</h2><p>Barik’s learning materials (lessons, scenes, translations, exercises, pictures, software) are © Barik and may not be copied without permission. Dictionary data from Wiktionary, with our changes, is under CC BY-SA 4.0; the classic texts are in the public domain; details are in “Sources and licences”.</p>',
